# CI test jobs (this repo)

Canon: [`.github/workflows/test-suite.yml`](../../.github/workflows/test-suite.yml).
`ci.yml` and `release.yml` **call** that workflow. Do not copy a second `dotnet test` matrix.

The repo is **public** — GitHub-hosted minutes are not the limit (~20 concurrent jobs are).
Do **not** fold CI back into one sequential `dotnet test` on the whole `.sln` to “save runners”.

## What may not run in one testhost

`[CollectionDefinition("AnalyzerLifecycle", DisableParallelization = true)]` plus
`AnalyzerShadowPublisher`: one MSBuild lifecycle host / shadow dirs. In-process
xUnit threads will race. Unit tests (`Category!=AnalyzerLifecycle`) already parallelize
inside the testhost.

## Partition contract

One OS runs two shards. Within that OS the shards must not overlap. On Windows their union is every discovered test. On Ubuntu `unit` also excludes `RequiresWindows` (the task-01 inventory, four tests). That exclusion is a filter, so those tests are absent from the Linux TRX (`notExecuted` stays 0). Do not put them back into the Linux filter and do not mark them `[Fact(Skip)]`.

| OS | Shard | Filter | `ROSLYN_MCP_ANALYZER_LIFECYCLE` |
|---|---|---|---|
| `windows` | `unit` | `Category!=AnalyzerLifecycle` | unset |
| `windows` | `lifecycle` | `Category=AnalyzerLifecycle` | `1` |
| `ubuntu` | `unit` | `Category!=AnalyzerLifecycle&Category!=RequiresWindows` | unset |
| `ubuntu` | `lifecycle` | `Category=AnalyzerLifecycle` | `1` |

Display names: `unit (windows)`, `lifecycle (windows)`, `unit (ubuntu)`, `lifecycle (ubuntu)`. Artifacts: `trx-unit-windows`, `trx-lifecycle-windows`, `trx-unit-ubuntu`, `trx-lifecycle-ubuntu`. Caller checks in `ci.yml` / `release.yml` are prefixed with `tests /`.

A red job on either OS fails the workflow. Do not put `continue-on-error` back on Ubuntu. The ten consecutive Linux main-suite runs that allowed that are recorded in `docs/linux-x64-support/evidence/task-02-linux-main-ten-runs.md`.

`AnalyzerLifecycleHostTests` is the **only** class carrying `Category=AnalyzerLifecycle`
(thirteen host methods). `Epoch1SemanticInventoryTests` is source-only, carries no trait, and
runs in `unit`. Do not add named per-epoch shards back, and do not leave an empty named shard.

`AnalyzerLifecycleFactAttribute` / `AnalyzerLifecycleTheoryAttribute` read the variable **before**
the host probe: anything other than `1` skips without starting an MSBuild host. MCP tools never set
it, so an agent must not pick these methods through `run_specific_test` — the run would skip.

`fail-fast: false`. Skip is a **job failure** (`.github/scripts/Assert-NoSkippedTests.ps1`), not a
green CI. Never weaken that script.

Pass `--filter` as a quoted env value (`"$env:FILTER"`). Bare `&` in PowerShell is the call operator.

JS actions must be Node 24 majors (`checkout@v6`, `setup-dotnet@v5`, `upload-artifact@v7`,
`download-artifact@v8`). Do not pin `@v4` of those — GitHub removes Node 20. Do not set
`ACTIONS_ALLOW_USE_UNSECURE_NODE_VERSION`. Hosted `windows-latest` is new enough.
